ull,"mstr_project_id":null,"OBJECTID":297257,"ocip_ind":null,"orig_cntrct_amt":null,"pct_complete":null,"pct_elapsed":null,"pdbs_proj_no":"S-R399(203)","pdl_desc":"Other Study","pdl_type":5,"pin":13163,"pin_desc":"Modeling for Project Prioritization","pin_stat_cd":"1","pin_stat_nm":"Closed","pin_status_phase_desc":"Closed","plan_amt":null,"planned_construction_year":2015,"pre_bid_mtg_dat":null,"primary_concept":"Traffic","prime":null,"priority_proj":"Y","proceed_dat":null,"program":"Other","proj_concpt_cd":"267","proj_concpt_nm":"Traffic","proj_delvr_mthd":"Other","proj_loc":"Region Wide","proj_route_seq":1,"proj_typ_nm":"Studies","proj_type":"STD","proj_xref_no":10625,"project_id":null,"project_manager":"SCHVANEVELDT, BRENT","project_objective":"1) PROJECT OBJECTIVE (BRIEF GOAL):\nUDOT Region 3 Project Prioritization Study Scope of Work\nAvenue Consultants (Avenue) will perform an analysis of a potential methodology to determine\ncongestion related benefits of planned projects. Using travel models each project to be evaluated will be\nmodeled and compared against a baseline to determine the relative benefit based on hours of delay\nreduction. The relative benefits of the analyzed projects will then be used to prioritize the projects for\ncongestion benefit. The scope of work is described below.\nTask 1 ¿ Project Management & Meetings\nThis task covers internal project management and meeting attendance. It is assumed that there will be\ntwo project meetings: one to finalize the projects to be evaluated and another to discuss the results of\nthe evaluation.\nTask 2 ¿ Urbanized Area Evaluation\nThe WFRC/MAG travel model will be used to evaluate a list of up to 20 urbanized area projects. These\nprojects will largely consist of those in Phase 1 of the MAG RTP although other projects or phasing of\nproject are likely to be included in the list. A transit project (or combination of transit projects) will also\nbe included in the list. The final list of projects to be evaluated will be determined in coordination with\nUDOT and MAG.\nThe horizon year for the analysis is assumed to be 2025 consistent with the end of Phase 1 of the\nupcoming 2015 RTP using draft land use forecasts. The baseline scenario will be the existing\ntransportation network plus funded projects. A full model run will be done for this scenario and the trip\ntables produced by that run will be used for all of the project runs. Summary tables comparing delay for\nAM, midday, PM, evening, and daily time periods will be produced.\nTask 3 ¿ Rural Area Evaluation\nThe Utah Statewide Travel Model (USTM) will be used to evaluate up to five projects, which would\ninclude rural projects that would presumably be in the Uintah Basin. The USTM is still a relatively new\nmodel that has not been widely used and may not be suitable for this type of analysis. This task will\nevaluate the suitability of USTM for use in the congestion benefit portion of the project prioritization\nprocess.\nSchedule\nThe urbanized area evaluation will be completed within two weeks of notice-to-proceed. This assumes\nthat the list of projects to be analyzed will be quickly developed. The rural area evaluation will require\nan additional week to complete.\nCost Estimate\nThe above scope of work is expected to require 114 hours of staff time to complete for a total labor cost\nof $13,269. Mileage travel expenses will be another $112, resulting in a total estimated cost of $13,381.\n\n2) WHERE TO FIND MORE INFORMATION (CONCEPT, ETC):\n\n\n3) RECOMMENDED TYPE DELIVERY AND CONSTRUCTION METHOD:\n\n\n4) PROJECT SPECIFIC COMMENTS AND EXPECTATIONS:\n\n\n5) FUNDING NOTES:\n\n","project_type":"CNTNGCY","project_value":22323.59,"projected_start_date":null,"pub_ctc_email":"bschvaneveldt@utah.gov","pub_ctc_nm":"SCHVANEVELDT, BRENT","pub_ctc_ph":"(801)227-8025","public_desc":"Traffic studies are a review of current traffic volumes and predicted future traffic volumes. The results of the studies are used to propose appropriate designs at intersections, interchanges and corridors.","public_desc_tag1":null,"public_desc_tag2":null,"public_desc_tag3":null,"public_desc_tag4":null,"public_desc_tag5":null,"re_cons_contact_email":null,"re_cons_contact_nm":null,"re_cons_contact_phone":null,"region_cd":"3","region_prty":333,"road_sys_cd":"NA","route_class":"OTHER","route_desc":"Non LRS Route - Point","route_dir_id":null,"route_id":null,"rr_crossings_included":"N","scoping_status_dt":"2014-08-19T00:00:00+00:00","secondary_concept":" ","sep_mstr_yn_typ":null,"sponsor_name":"UTAH DEPT. OF TRANSPORTATION","st_fed_ind":"S","state_dollars":22323.59,"stimulus_flag":null,"stip_sponsor_cd":"UDOT","stip_workshop":"N","stip_workshop_approved_amt":null,"stip_workshop_approved_dt":null,"stip_workshop_yr":null,"submit_for_advertise_date":"2014-10-02T17:00:00+00:00","substantially_complete_date":null,"test_project_flag":null,"tif_plan_fund_cd":null,"tif_priority_flag":"N","tif_priority_score_range":null,"tip_cd":"UDOT","to_pin":null,"total_cd_amount":0,"total_expenditures":22323.59,"udot_resident_engineer":null,"unified_plan_unique_id_lst":null,"uom_typ":null,"up_phase":333,"up_project_id":null,"use_geom_only_ind":"N","will_advertise_flag":"N","work_cal_typ":null,"workshop_cat":null,"start_dat":null,"epm_plan_end_date":null}},{"attributes":{"abandoned_flag":"Y","advertise_date":null,"avail_awrd_fnd_amt":null,"award_dat":null,"awrdd_cntrctr_company_emp_id":null,"beg_mileage":342.727,"bid_open_dat":null,"change_order_amt":null,"cnslt_resident_engineer":null,"cnty_cd":"49","cnty_name":"UTAH","comm_aprv_ind":"N","comments":"Closed per state final voucher dated 2/9/2018.  Closing amount: $272,815.72","commit_for_advertise_date":"2015-07-31T00:00:00+00:00","concept_desc":"Traffic Signal - New","contract_range":"$0-$500,000","created_by":"MWATSONUDOT","created_dt":"2014-04-01T09:20:07+00:00","current_mod_date":"2019-08-15T00:00:00+00:00","days":null,"design_engineer":"J-U-B ENGINEERS, INC.","dsnbld_ind":nul